Verdict: SUPPORTED
Rationale: The claim states that the sub-units using two types of RNA are major components of the unit consisting of Ribosomal protein. Evidence supports that ribosomes are composed of ribosomal RNA (rRNA) and ribosomal proteins, and that rRNA binds to ribosomal proteins to form subunits. Additionally, the two types of RNA (rRNA and tRNA) are involved in protein synthesis, with rRNA forming part of the ribosome structure and tRNA delivering amino acids. No evidence contradicts the claim, and all material parts are sufficiently supported.
Rounds: 5, findings: 10
